{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "DudhiaSW",
  "description": "The Dudhia (1989) shortwave radiation scheme of WRF (ra_sw_physics = 1, SUBROUTINE SWPARA of phys/module_ra_sw.F, WRF 4.8) as a single-column component on the EarthSciDiscretizations grids/column_nonuniform_1d grid (layer index `lev`, layer 1 at the surface; interface index `lev_nodes`, interface 1 the surface, interface NLEV+1 the top of the atmosphere). The scheme is a single downward pass of the direct solar beam S(z) that is depleted by four processes: absorption by water vapour, absorption by cloud, reflection by cloud, and Rayleigh/aerosol scattering. The first three are functions of CUMULATIVE slant paths from the top of the atmosphere, written here as the integrals W(z) = int_z^top rho q_l,eff dz (effective liquid water path, q_l,eff = qc + 0.1 qi + 0.05 qr + 0.02 qs + 0.05 qg) and U(z) = int_z^top rho qv dz (water-vapour path), lowered by the grid's integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top rule: the vapour absorptance A_v(U/mu) is the Lacis-Hansen (1974) fit, the cloud reflectance R_c(mu, alw) and absorptance A_c(mu, alw) are Stephens (1978) tables in alw = log10(W/(mu 1 g/m^2) + 1), and a layer's fractional contribution is the downward increment of each cumulative function across the layer (SWPARA: TOTABS-OLDABS, ALBA-OLDALB, ABSC-OLDABC, clamped at 0). Scattering is a per-layer fraction cssca rho dz / mu. The beam itself is a genuinely sequential sweep (esm-spec 4.3.1.1 recurrence), because SWPARA applies each layer's fraction not to S but to partial beams -- vapour absorption to the beam depleted only by cloud and scattering, cloud reflection/absorption to the beam depleted only by scattering and vapour -- which SWPARA bookkeeps with the running sums DABS, DSCLD, DSCA. Using SWPARA's exact identity S_top(k) = S_toa - DSCLD - DSCA - DABS these partial beams are S_top + D_vap and S_top + D_cld, so the running sums obey the LINEAR recurrences D_vap(n) = (1 + a_n) D_vap(n-1) + a_n S(n) and D_cld(n) = (1 + c_n) D_cld(n-1) + c_n S(n), whose variation-of-constants solutions D(n) = G(n) sum_{j<n} x_j S(j)/G(j+1), G(n) = prod_{i<n} (1 + x_i), are substituted into the S recurrence. This leaves ONE causal self-reference (S_dn) with two non-recursive growth factors, which is what the format admits: the esm-spec forbids an edge between two distinct recurrence variables (a cycle), so the three coupled Fortran accumulators cannot be written as three mutually-referencing recurrences (see the Spike B report). The sweep runs top-down, i.e. against the lev index, and a recurrence folds only ascending, so the sweep variables live on the reversed index sets lev_down / lev_down_nodes (m = 1 the top layer, n = 1 the top of the atmosphere) and are mapped back by the reversal templates; all physics fields stay on lev / lev_nodes (lev_down: m = 1 the top layer, lev = NLEV + 1 - m; lev_down_nodes: n = 1 the top of the atmosphere, lev_nodes = NLEV + 2 - n; layer m lies between nodes m and m + 1). The heating rate is written as the flux divergence of the cumulative ABSORBED flux Phi_abs(z) (vapour + cloud absorption above z, an interface field that is 0 at the top): rho cp dT/dt = -d Phi_abs/dz, lowered by face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces; the reflected and scattered parts leave the column without heating it, exactly as in SWPARA, and the surface absorbs (1 - albedo) S(surface). The theta tendency is dT/dt divided by the Exner function (SWRAD: RTHRATEN = RTHRATEN + TTEN1D/PI3D). Night: SWPARA returns all-zero when cos(zenith) <= 1e-9 or the top-of-atmosphere irradiance <= 1e-9 W/m^2; here the sweep is evaluated with the formal value mu = 1 at night (a near-zero mu would overflow the 1/mu slant paths) and the outputs gsw, dT/dt, dtheta/dt carry the factor `daylight`, so a night column yields exactly zero heating and surface flux while the internals are formal. NOT transcribed (all asserted inactive or absent in the reference regimes): the renormalisation applied when a single layer would deplete more than 99 % of the beam (TRANS0 < 1: FF = 99/(...), a numerical guard that couples the four fractions to the beam and cannot be expressed without a second self-reference), the 1e-9 W/m^2 floor on S (SDOWN = AMAX1(1.E-9, ...)), the WRF-Chem aerosol optical depth terms (aer_dry1, aer_water1, zero without chemistry; the aerosol absorption XABSA is identically 0 in SWPARA), and the slope_rad/shadow topographic correction of the surface flux. Reference tests: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column dumps replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) standalone kernels/sw_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, tolerances documented per test. Transcribed guards: negative increments clipped to 0, the table argument clamp alw_max, the renormalisation of a layer whose raw depletion exceeds 1 - tau_min (ff, tau) and the beam floor S_min. Validity of the closed forms below a renormalised layer: see S_dn and n_renorm. Not transcribed: the slope-dependent radiation option (slope_rad) and aerosol absorption (XABSA = 0 in WRF 4.8).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "radiation",
   "shortwave",
   "dudhia",
   "column",
   "ra_sw_physics=1"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Dudhia, J. (1989). Numerical study of convection observed during the Winter Monsoon Experiment using a mesoscale two-dimensional model. J. Atmos. Sci. 46, 3077-3107.",
    "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1989)046<3077:NSOCOD>2.0.CO;2"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Lacis, A. A. and Hansen, J. E. (1974). A parameterization for the absorption of solar radiation in the Earth's atmosphere. J. Atmos. Sci. 31, 118-133.",
    "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1974)031<0118:APFTAO>2.0.CO;2"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Stephens, G. L. (1978). Radiation profiles in extended water clouds. II: Parameterization schemes. J. Atmos. Sci. 35, 2123-2132.",
    "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1978)035<2123:RPIEWC>2.0.CO;2"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Technical Note NCAR/TN-556+STR, section 8.3 (Dudhia shortwave).",
    "doi": "10.5065/1dfh-6p97"
   },
   {
    "citation": "wrf-model/WRF v4.8.0 phys/module_ra_sw.F (SWRAD, SWPARA, swinit); instrumented copy in ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "lev_down": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NLEV"
  },
  "lev_down_nodes": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "NLEV",
     1
    ]
   }
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "DudhiaSW": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_thermo.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "./lacis_hansen_absorptance.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "./stephens_cloud_tables.esm"
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    },
    "par": {
     "ref": "./dudhia_sw_parameters.esm"
    }
   },
   "expression_templates": {
    "downward_increment": {
     "params": [
      "G"
     ],
     "description": "Increment of a cumulative-from-the-top interface field G across each layer, G[k] - G[k+1] (bottom minus top): the layer's own contribution to a quantity accumulated downward from the top of the atmosphere.",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "G"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "-",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "G",
          "k"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "G",
          {
           "op": "+",
           "args": [
            "k",
            1
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "to_top_down_layers": {
     "params": [
      "F"
     ],
     "description": "Reverse a layer field from lev (surface up) to lev_down (top down): F_dn[m] = F[NLEV + 1 - m].",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "m"
      ],
      "args": [
       "F"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "m": {
        "from": "lev_down"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "F",
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "+",
           "args": [
            "NLEV",
            1
           ]
          },
          "m"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "to_bottom_up_layers": {
     "params": [
      "F"
     ],
     "description": "Reverse a layer field from lev_down (top down) to lev (surface up): F[k] = F_dn[NLEV + 1 - k].",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "F"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "F",
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "+",
           "args": [
            "NLEV",
            1
           ]
          },
          "k"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "to_bottom_up_nodes": {
     "params": [
      "G"
     ],
     "description": "Reverse an interface field from lev_down_nodes (top down) to lev_nodes (surface up): G[kn] = G_dn[NLEV + 2 - kn].",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "kn"
      ],
      "args": [
       "G"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "kn": {
        "from": "lev_nodes"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "G",
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "+",
           "args": [
            "NLEV",
            2
           ]
          },
          "kn"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "growth_factor": {
     "params": [
      "x"
     ],
     "description": "Homogeneous solution of the linear depletion recurrence D(n) = (1 + x_n) D(n-1) + x_n S(n): G[n] = prod_{i<n} (1 + x[i]) over the layers above node n (G[1] = 1 at the top of the atmosphere).",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "n"
      ],
      "reduce": "*",
      "args": [
       "x"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "n": {
        "from": "lev_down_nodes"
       },
       "i": {
        "from": "lev_down"
       }
      },
      "filter": {
       "op": "<",
       "args": [
        "i",
        "n"
       ]
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "+",
       "args": [
        1.0,
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "x",
          "i"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "accumulated_depletion": {
     "params": [
      "G",
      "x"
     ],
     "description": "Variation-of-constants solution of D(n) = (1 + x_n) D(n-1) + x_n S(n), D(1) = 0: the flux removed from the beam above node n by the process with layer fractions x, D[n] = G[n] sum_{j<n} x[j] S_dn[j] / G[j+1], reading the swept beam S_dn.",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "n"
      ],
      "reduce": "+",
      "args": [
       "G",
       "x",
       "S_dn"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "n": {
        "from": "lev_down_nodes"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "lev_down"
       }
      },
      "filter": {
       "op": "<",
       "args": [
        "j",
        "n"
       ]
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "G",
            "n"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "x",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "S_dn",
            "j"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "G",
          {
           "op": "+",
           "args": [
            "j",
            1
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "cumulative_from_top": {
     "params": [
      "F"
     ],
     "description": "Running sum of a top-down layer field over the layers above node n: C[n] = sum_{j<n} F[j] (C[1] = 0).",
     "body": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "n"
      ],
      "reduce": "+",
      "args": [
       "F"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "n": {
        "from": "lev_down_nodes"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "lev_down"
       }
      },
      "filter": {
       "op": "<",
       "args": [
        "j",
        "n"
       ]
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "F",
        "j"
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "csza": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.5,
     "description": "Cosine of the solar zenith angle (WRF coszen)."
    },
    "albedo": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.2,
     "description": "Surface albedo."
    },
    "solcon": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 1370.0,
     "description": "Solar constant corrected for the Earth-Sun distance (WRF solcon)."
    },
    "obscur": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Solar-eclipse obscuration fraction (WRF obscur); 0 outside eclipses."
    },
    "cssca": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/kg",
     "default": 1e-05,
     "description": "Clear-sky (Rayleigh + background aerosol) scattering coefficient per unit air mass path, namelist swrad_scat * 1e-5 (swinit); 1e-5 m^2/kg for swrad_scat = 1."
    },
    "icloud": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Cloud switch (namelist icloud): 1 includes the condensate in the effective liquid water path, 0 sets it to zero."
    },
    "ze": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Interface heights above ground, ze[1] = 0, consumer-supplied through `input_ze` (the cumulative sum of the WRF layer thicknesses dz8w); the grid's single geometry input."
    },
    "zc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer mid-point heights, grid-derived from ze."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer thicknesses (WRF dz8w), grid-derived from ze; the measure of the column integrals and of the flux divergence."
    },
    "T": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer temperature (WRF t3d); the prognostic state, initialised from `input_T` and heated by dTdt."
    },
    "p": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer pressure (WRF p3d), consumer-supplied through `input_p`."
    },
    "exner": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Exner function (WRF pi3d), consumer-supplied through `input_exner`; converts the temperature tendency to a theta tendency."
    },
    "qv": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Water-vapour mixing ratio (WRF qv3d), through `input_qv`."
    },
    "qc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio (WRF qc3d), through `input_qc`."
    },
    "qr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Rain-water mixing ratio (WRF qr3d), through `input_qr`."
    },
    "qi": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud-ice mixing ratio (WRF qi3d), through `input_qi`."
    },
    "qs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Snow mixing ratio (WRF qs3d), through `input_qs`."
    },
    "qg": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Graupel mixing ratio (WRF qg3d), through `input_qg`."
    },
    "rho": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Dry-air density p/(r_d T) recomputed by the scheme (SWPARA RO)."
    },
    "soltop": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Top-of-atmosphere irradiance normal to the beam, solcon (1 - obscur) (SWPARA SOLTOP)."
    },
    "daylight": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 when the scheme is active (csza > mu_min and soltop > soltop_min), 0 at night or total eclipse (SWPARA's early return)."
    },
    "mu": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Cosine of the solar zenith angle used in the slant paths: csza by day (SWPARA XMU = CSZA on the day branch) and the formal value 1 at night, so that every internal stays finite and benign when the outputs are masked (a value near WRF's 1e-9 threshold would make the 1/mu slant paths overflow the sweep)."
    },
    "S_toa": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Downward solar flux on a horizontal surface at the top of the atmosphere, soltop mu (SWPARA SDOWN(1))."
    },
    "lwc_eff": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Effective condensed-water content rho (qc + w_ice qi + w_rain qr + w_snow qs + w_graupel qg), switched by icloud; the integrand of the liquid water path (SWPARA XLWP / DZ, in kg/m^3 instead of g/m^3)."
    },
    "wvc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Water-vapour content rho qv, the integrand of the vapour path (SWPARA XWVP / DZ)."
    },
    "m_air": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Air mass path of the layer rho dz (SWPARA XATP)."
    },
    "W": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Effective liquid water path above each interface, W(z) = int_z^top lwc_eff dz (SWPARA WW at the bottom of each layer; 0 at the top of the atmosphere)."
    },
    "U": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Water-vapour path above each interface, U(z) = int_z^top rho qv dz (SWPARA UV; 0 at the top)."
    },
    "alw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Stephens table argument log10(W/(mu w_ref) + 1) with the slant path in g/m^2, clamped at alw_max (SWPARA ALW)."
    },
    "R_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Cumulative cloud reflectance of the cloud above each interface, Stephens table at (mu, alw[kn]) (SWPARA ALBA / 100). Written as an explicit gather over lev_nodes because the closed function interp.bilinear is scalar and the runners do not broadcast it over an array argument."
    },
    "A_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Cumulative cloud absorptance of the cloud above each interface (SWPARA ABSC / 100)."
    },
    "A_vap": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Cumulative water-vapour absorptance of the vapour above each interface, Lacis-Hansen fit at the slant path U/(mu u_ref) in g/cm^2 (SWPARA TOTABS)."
    },
    "da_vap": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Vapour absorptance increment across each layer, max(0, A_vap[k] - A_vap[k+1]) (SWPARA TOTABS - OLDABS, XABS >= 0)."
    },
    "dr_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud reflectance increment across each layer, max(0, R_cld[k] - R_cld[k+1]) (SWPARA (ALBA - OLDALB)/100, XALB >= 0)."
    },
    "da_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud absorptance increment across each layer, max(0, A_cld[k] - A_cld[k+1]) (SWPARA (ABSC - OLDABC)/100, XABSC >= 0)."
    },
    "f_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Total cloud depletion fraction of the layer, dr_cld + da_cld, applied to the beam depleted only by scattering and vapour (SWPARA (XALB + XABSC)/100 before the beam ratio)."
    },
    "f_sca": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Rayleigh/aerosol scattering fraction of the layer, cssca m_air / mu (SWPARA XSCA)."
    },
    "a_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "da_vap in sweep (top-down) order."
    },
    "c_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "f_cld in sweep order."
    },
    "b_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "da_cld in sweep order."
    },
    "r_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "dr_cld in sweep order."
    },
    "s_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "f_sca in sweep order."
    },
    "G_vap": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Growth factor prod_{i<n} (1 + a_dn[i]) of the vapour-absorption bookkeeping recurrence."
    },
    "G_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Growth factor prod_{i<n} (1 + c_dn[i]) of the cloud-depletion bookkeeping recurrence."
    },
    "S_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "The swept downward beam at each interface, top-down: S_dn[1] = S_toa, S_dn[n] = max(S_min, max(tau_min S_dn[n-1], S_dn[n-1] (1 - a - c - s)_{n-1} - a_{n-1} D_vap[n-1] - c_{n-1} D_cld[n-1])), with the depletions above node n-1 in closed form (SWPARA SDOWN(K+1) = AMAX1(1.E-9, SDOWN(K)*TRANS0*0.01) with TRANS0 floored at 1 %: the inner max is the layer transmissivity floor tau_min, the outer max the beam floor S_min). The one causal self-reference of the component (esm-spec 4.3.1.1): a two-stream-like downward pass whose next value depends on the whole beam history through the partial-beam bookkeeping. VALIDITY: the closed forms of D_vap and D_cld assume SWPARA's bookkeeping identity SDOWN(K) = SDOWN(1) - DSCLD - DSCA - DABS, which holds down to and including the first renormalised layer (SWPARA keeps accumulating the RAW, unrescaled fractions in DSCLD/DSCA/DABS, so below a renormalised layer the identity is off by the renormalisation deficit and the per-layer fractions there depend on a coupled four-component sweep S, DSCLD, DSCA, DABS that esm-spec 4.3.1.1 cannot express (only the array being defined may be read causally; see data/eqwefic/esm-repro/spikeB/probe_vector_recurrence.esm). The component is therefore exact when every renormalised layer has no cloud- or vapour-depleting layer below it; n_renorm and the test regimes make this explicit."
    },
    "D_vap_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Flux absorbed by water vapour above node n (SWPARA DABS), closed form of its bookkeeping recurrence."
    },
    "D_cld_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Flux removed by cloud (reflection + absorption) above node n (SWPARA DSCLD)."
    },
    "D_sca_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Flux scattered out of the beam above node n (SWPARA DSCA)."
    },
    "F_vap_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "Flux absorbed by water vapour in layer m: a_dn (S_dn + D_vap_dn), the absorptance increment times the beam depleted only by cloud and scattering (SWPARA XABS*SDOWN)."
    },
    "F_cabs_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "Flux absorbed by cloud in layer m: b_dn (S_dn + D_cld_dn) (SWPARA XABSC*SDOWN/100)."
    },
    "F_cref_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "Flux reflected by cloud in layer m: r_dn (S_dn + D_cld_dn) (SWPARA XALB*SDOWN/100)."
    },
    "F_sca_dn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_down"
     ],
     "description": "Flux scattered out of the beam in layer m: s_dn S_dn (SWPARA XSCA*SDOWN)."
    },
    "S": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Downward solar beam at each interface (SWPARA SDOWN, reversed): S[NLEV+1] = S_toa, S[1] the flux reaching the surface."
    },
    "Phi_abs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Cumulative absorbed flux above each interface, Phi_abs(z) = int_z^top q_abs dz' (vapour + cloud absorption after the renormalisation), 0 at the top of the atmosphere; the layer heating is its downward increment, so rho cp dT/dt = -d Phi_abs/dz."
    },
    "D_vap": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "D_vap_dn on lev_nodes (SWPARA DABS at the bottom of each layer)."
    },
    "D_cld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "D_cld_dn on lev_nodes (SWPARA DSCLD)."
    },
    "D_sca": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "D_sca_dn on lev_nodes (SWPARA DSCA)."
    },
    "F_vap": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Flux absorbed by water vapour in each layer, on lev."
    },
    "F_cabs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Flux absorbed by cloud in each layer, on lev."
    },
    "F_cref": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Flux reflected by cloud in each layer, on lev."
    },
    "F_sca": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Flux scattered out of the beam in each layer, on lev."
    },
    "S_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Beam entering each layer from above, S[k+1] (SWPARA SDOWN(K) for the layer being processed)."
    },
    "f_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Raw depletion fraction of the layer, (F_vap + F_cabs + F_cref + F_sca)/S_top: the sum of the four per-layer fractions SWPARA computes before its renormalisation (XALB + XABSC + 100 XABS + 100 XSCA, in per cent)."
    },
    "tau_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Raw layer transmissivity 1 - f_raw (SWPARA TRANS0/100 before the renormalisation test); may be negative for an optically very thick layer."
    },
    "ff": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Renormalisation factor of the layer's depletion fractions: 1 where tau_raw >= tau_min, else (1 - tau_min)/f_raw so that the rescaled fractions sum to 1 - tau_min (SWPARA FF = 99./(XALB + XABSC + XABS*100. + XSCA*100.)). The rescaled fractions are what SWPARA applies to the beam and the heating; the cumulative depletions D_* keep the raw values."
    },
    "xabs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer vapour absorption as a fraction of the entering beam, F_vap/S_top (SWPARA XABS), after the renormalisation: ff times the raw fraction."
    },
    "xabsc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer cloud absorption as a fraction of the entering beam (SWPARA XABSC/100), after the renormalisation: ff times the raw fraction."
    },
    "xalb": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer cloud reflection as a fraction of the entering beam (SWPARA XALB/100), after the renormalisation: ff times the raw fraction."
    },
    "xsca": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer scattering as a fraction of the entering beam (SWPARA XSCA; identical to f_sca), after the renormalisation: ff times the raw fraction."
    },
    "tau": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer transmissivity actually applied to the beam, max(tau_raw, tau_min) (SWPARA TRANS0/100 after the IF(TRANS0.LT.1.) block sets it to 1 %)."
    },
    "q_abs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Volumetric shortwave absorption of the layer, ff (F_vap + F_cabs)/dz: the applied (renormalised) vapour plus cloud absorption per unit volume (SWPARA SDOWN(K)*(XABSC + XABS*100.)*0.01/DZ(K) after the renormalisation)."
    },
    "dTdt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Shortwave heating rate, -daylight D(Phi_abs, lev)/(rho cp) (SWPARA TTEN)."
    },
    "dthdt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Potential-temperature tendency dTdt/exner (SWRAD's increment of RTHRATEN)."
    },
    "gsw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Net shortwave flux absorbed at the surface, daylight (1 - albedo) S[1] (SWPARA GSW)."
    },
    "n_renorm": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Number of layers whose depletion fractions were renormalised (tau_raw < tau_min) while the scheme is active (0 at night). The component is exact only when no depleting layer lies below a renormalised one (see S_dn); the tests assert n_renorm = 0 for the SCM regimes and 1, in the lowest layer, for the fog regime."
    },
    "n_floor": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Number of interfaces at which the daytime beam sits on its floor S_min (SWPARA AMAX1(1.E-9, ...); 0 at night); reached only below about six consecutive renormalised layers, a regime outside the component's validity (see S_dn), so the tests assert n_floor = 0."
    }
