   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "scm_call1_morning_clear",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, swrad_scat = 1, icloud = 1) dumped by the instrumented fork (module_esm_dump, SWRAD/SWPARA hooks) and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) standalone kernels/sw_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork; inputs are the dumped SWRAD arguments (single-precision values widened) of tile column 1, and every expected value is the real64 replay (the same inputs through the same Fortran in binary64, so the scheme's constants and literals are exact and the only residual is evaluation-order roundoff). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step), so no small-dt replay is involved. Column assertions are Linf_error of the whole field against the inline reference (WRF's top-down arrays reversed onto lev/lev_nodes, the top-of-atmosphere interface appended as 0 for the cumulative fields, per-cent quantities divided by 100, g/m^2 paths converted to kg/m^2); spot checks use a relative tolerance. Tolerances: measured Linf mismatch between this component and the real64 replay over all six regimes is at binary64 roundoff -- S and the cumulative depletions <= 1.2e-12 W/m^2 (1e-15 relative), U <= 4e-15 kg/m^2, W <= 1e-16 kg/m^2, the dimensionless absorptances/reflectances and layer fractions <= 4e-15, heating rates <= 1.3e-18 K/s -- so the column tolerances are set at about 1e-9 of each field's column maximum (S, D_*: abs 1e-6 W/m^2; U: 1e-8 kg/m^2; W: 1e-12 kg/m^2; rho: 1e-9 kg/m^3; m_air: 1e-7 kg/m^2; fractions: abs 1e-9; dT/dt, dtheta/dt: 1e-13 K/s), i.e. the 1e-9 relative contract for double-precision references, roughly a million times the measured error; scalar spot checks use rel 1e-9. Regime: first radiation call of the run (call 1, 19:00 UTC = 12:34 LST, cos zenith 0.629), no condensate at all (qc = qr = qs = qg = 0, qi = 0): pure clear-sky vapour absorption and scattering, the cloud tables return 0 everywhere, gsw = 542 W/m^2.",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "csza": 0.6286112070083618,
         "albedo": 0.20000000298023224,
         "solcon": 1384.3160400390625,
         "obscur": 0.0,
         "cssca": 9.999999747378752e-06,
         "icloud": 1.0
       },
       "expression_template_imports": [
         {
           "ref": "./tests/scm_call1_morning_clear_inputs.esm"
         }
       ],
       "time_span": {
         "start": 0,
         "end": 1
       },
       "assertions": [
         {
           "variable": "daylight",
           "time": 0.0,
           "expected": 1.0,
           "tolerance": {
             "abs": 0.0
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "S_toa",
           "time": 0.0,
           "expected": 870.1965768099908,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-09
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "gsw",
           "time": 0.0,
           "expected": 542.4128734982716,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-09
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "rho",
           "time": 0.0,
           "reduce": "Linf_error",
           "expected": 0.0,
           "reference": {
             "op": "aggregate",
             "output_idx": [
               "k"
             ],
             "args": [],
             "ranges": {
               "k": {
                 "from": "lev"
               }
             },
             "expr": {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                 {
